7. Alignment prior to Variant calling
For variant calling Sniffles can be used with any aligner, we went ahead using Minimap2 with the following commands to create BAM files.

$ minimap2 -ax map-ont GCA_001857865ref.fa Ss07.fasta > Ss07.aligned.sam

$ samtools view -Sb Ss07.aligned.sam > Ss07.aligned.bam

$ samtools sort Ss07.aligned.bam -o Ss07.aligned.sorted.bam

$ samtools index Ss07.aligned.sorted.bam

*******Here I jus noticed an error consisting in that the alignment was done using fasta files which might have played a role in some issues and inaccuracies with the identification of SVs.

So had to re run this step, see the new code used with FASTQ files this time.

ALIGNMENT PRIOR TO VARIANT CALLING WITH Minimap2 ****RE RUN * *

$ minimap2 -ax map-ont GCA_001857865ref.fa barcode07_concatenated.fastq > Ss07aligned.sam $ samtools view -Sb Ss07aligned.sam > Ss07aligned.bam $ samtools sort Ss07aligned.bam -o Ss07aligned.sorted.bam $ samtools index Ss07aligned.sorted.bam

$ minimap2 -ax map-ont GCA_001857865ref.fa barcode12_concatenated.fastq > Ss12aligned.sam $ samtools view -Sb Ss12aligned.sam > Ss12aligned.bam $ samtools sort Ss12aligned.bam -o Ss12aligned.sorted.bam $ samtools index Ss12aligned.sorted.bam

8. SV calling with Sniffles.
Installation

$ pip install sniffles

Ran with their specific commands (Described below). I did individual (1), and also with multiple calling (2)

So, when I type $ sniffles in the CL I can see a couple of options.

I used the command displayed in option A (Call SVs for single sample):
~$ sniffles --input sorted_indexed_alignments.bam --vcf output.vcf (This is the command displayed in Github sniffles page among a couple others)

~$ sniffles --input Ss07.aligned.sorted.bam -v variants.vcf (This is the actual command I used for each of our samples).

I used the command displayed in option B (Multi-sample calling): 
Two step proces:

Step 1. Create .snf for each sample: sniffles --input sample1.bam --snf sample1.snf

Step 2. Combined calling: sniffles --input sample1.snf sample2.snf ... sampleN.snf --vcf multisample.vcf
Output from sniffles is a file in .vcf format

At this point I notified Valerio and Marysia of the mistake with using FASTQ files and that I added filters to generate the new vcf files, the following command describe the flag/commands used in Variant calling. The previously used multi-sample calling here was not performed as we are analyzing only two genomes.

$ sniffles --input Ss07aligned.sorted.bam --vcf PSVariants07.vcf --minsupport 10 --minsvlen 50 --qc-stdev-abs-max 500 --qc-coverage 5 --qc-strand True --long-ins-length 500 --long-del-length 10

$ sniffles --input Ss12aligned.sorted.bam --vcf PSVariants12.vcf --minsupport 10 --minsvlen 50 --qc-stdev-abs-max 500 --qc-coverage 5 --qc-strand True --long-ins-length 500 --long-del-length 10

Now I have new vcf files that were created with some filters and adequately priorly aligned with Minimap2 using fastq files now.

Custom Filters for Sniffles SV calling - The filters were intended to improve confidence and biological relevance of SVs in our fungal genomes

--min_support (5-10) I chose 10 meaning it requires 10 reads to support a variant for it to be reported. This is suggested to help reduce false positives from sequencing noise while retaining variants in lower coverage regions. (Some limitations though, while it reduces the false positives might miss low-frequency or heterozygous SVs in lower coverage regions. --min_length (50 bp) removes very small insertions/deletions that may be SNP/indel-level artifacts; focuses on true SVs. --qc-stdev-abs-max 500 Filters out SVs with excesive read variation (based on standard deviation of the SV region); limits noise from low-complexity/repetitive regions. --qc-coverage 5 Minimum average coverage for a variant to be called. Helps avoid false positives in poorly covered regions. --qc-strand True Requires strand bias check to ensure SVs are supported both forward and reverse reads- improves confidence. --long-ins-length 500 treshold for long insertions; variants longer that this are processed difrerently --long-del-length 10 Defines threshold for long deletions (low value means capturing most deletions as long variants)

This is so far:

